// `sort.max` and `sort.min` have no element to return from an empty list and
// no honest way to invent one, so they trap -- the same answer `xs[0]` gives
// to the same question. An `Option` return would put a `match` at every call
// site to handle a case most callers have already ruled out.
import sort;

List<int> empty = [];
print(sort.max(empty, (int a, int b) => a - b));
